    "VINIT: Initialize the void — pre-emission state where no ultra-high-energy proton exists in the observable volume",
    "IMSCRIB: Establish Lorentz-invariant self-identity — the proton's rest mass and charge are frame-independent constants",
    "AFWD: Emit and propagate — the proton travels from its unknown astrophysical source through intergalactic magnetic fields toward Earth",
    "CLINK: Compose propagation segments — each deflection and energy loss step chains to the next across ~100 Mpc",
    "FSPLIT: First atmospheric interaction — the proton collides with a nitrogen/oxygen nucleus at ~15 km altitude, forking into hadronic and electromagnetic arms",
    "EVALT: Affirm hadronic arm — charged pions decay to muons, neutral pions feed EM arm, nuclear fragments continue hadronic cascade",
    "AFWD: Propagate hadronic arm — muons travel to ground with minimal energy loss; hadronic core continues nuclear interactions",
    "CLINK: Chain hadronic interaction lengths — each nuclear collision produces next generation of secondaries",
    "EVALF: Affirm electromagnetic arm — π⁰→γγ initiates pair production and bremsstrahlung cascade in radiation lengths",
    "AFWD: Propagate electromagnetic arm — exponential growth to shower maximum at ~8 km, then attenuation",
    "CLINK: Chain electromagnetic radiation lengths — each generation doubles particles until critical energy reached",
    "ENGAGR: Hold composition paradice — measured muon count and shower fluctuations simultaneously affirm proton and iron primaries (B-state)",
    "FFUSE: Rejoin at detector — hadronic muons and electromagnetic e±/γ arrive simultaneously at Fly's Eye mirrors",
    "AREV: Reverse reconstruct — from ground signal infer primary energy (3.2×10²⁰ eV) and arrival direction via time-reversed shower model",
    "⋈: Medium-fidelity measurement — energy and direction reconstructed reliably; composition and source remain uncertain",
    "IFIX: Fix event record — write the 1991 October 15 event to permanent archival storage",
    "TANCH: Close at detector aperture — the Fly's Eye acceptance boundary terminates the process; no further propagation possible",
    "IMSCRIB: Close self-referential loop — the recorded event now exists as its own reference for all future UHECR studies"
  ],
