    "compiler": "Standard Model cross-sections + QGSJET/EPOS hadronic models + CORSIKA shower simulation + Fly's Eye detector response",
    "ipc": "Particle cascades communicate via energy-momentum conservation at each vertex; detector channels communicate via optical fiber timing and ADC readout",
    "memory": "Atmosphere acts as transient analog memory (shower development); magnetic tape provides permanent digital memory (event record)",
    "scheduler": "Causal ordering by light-cone propagation: emission → propagation → first interaction → cascade steps → ground arrival → trigger → readout → recording",
    "alfs": "The 1991 Fly's Eye event record (Run 2721, Event 1447) — the canonical bootstrap for all UHECR physics above 10²⁰ eV"
  },
  "entropy": {
    "cost": "~3×10²⁰ eV primary energy dissipated as ionization, heat, Cherenkov light, and neutrinos; ~10⁴ J deposited in atmosphere",
    "pre": "Single coherent ultra-high-energy proton in near-vacuum intergalactic space; low entropy, high free energy",
    "post": "Billions of thermalized secondary particles distributed across km-scale atmospheric volume; permanent bit record in detector archive",
    "verdict": "ΔS ≈ 0 — The cascade is a reversible unitary evolution (Liouville) until measurement; the IFIX step pays Landauer cost to fix one bit of cosmic-ray history, balanced by the enormous entropy production in the atmosphere"
  }
